// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/t27os/homes.t27 -- the HOMES of t27: which product each agent and each widget belongs to, and the
; tab T27 OS draws for each home. One registry; T27 OS reads its tabs from here.
; Owner, 2026-10-20: study all our agents and their homes -- t27a, t27b, t27c, t27u (the university with
; all its courses), t27t (our own model's training), and any other -- and link every widget to its home.
; Evidence, read on 2026-10-20 (nothing here is invented; what could not be established is named):
; - Homes with a law of their own: t27a specs/isa/t27a.t27; t27b cli/t27b/README.md (the native compiler,
;   `t27b test|build|verilog`); t27c bootstrap/src/compiler.rs (the bootstrap compiler, sealed by
;   bootstrap/stage0/FROZEN_HASH) with `t27c silicon|verdict|bench-agent`; t27f specs/t27f/frontend.t27;
;   t27o specs/tools/t27o/rust_convert.t27 (AGENTS.md: converts foreign code into .t27); t27t
;   specs/t27t/t27t.t27 (AGENTS.md "t27t: the t27 trainer", `tri t27t`); t27u gHashTag/trinity
;   apps/website/specs/course/courses.t27 (7 courses of 27 lessons).
; - Not homes, and why: t27os is the host that draws the tabs (it owns no product another home lacks);
;   t27mcp is the service half of T27F and TRI CLAW (specs/t27mcp/service.t27 decides by prefix which
;   tools it serves; its `home_of` is about MCP tool names, not about this registry).
; - The eighth home, QUEEN: the shared home. The Queen (agent T, specs/queen, specs/t27os/queen.t27) is the
;   orchestrator, and the agents that serve every home equally (governance, memory, metrics, scheduling,
;   security) have no single product; they live with her rather than in a gap.
; - Letters are NOT homes: agent B is Beta (Build), not t27b; agent U is Upsilon (Universe levels), not the
;   university t27u; agent I is the ISA, which is why it sits in t27a.
; - Widgets: the 195 ids of the t27 widget gallery (gHashTag/trinity apps/website/specs/widgets/gallery.t27),
;   by index in gallery order. A widget belongs to the home whose product emits what it shows: bitstream,
;   fasm, pins, JTAG, timing, Verilog and every `t27c-` page are t27c's; GoldenFloat and training pieces
;   are t27t's; a lesson widget that exists only for a course (basics-*, golden-*) is t27u's; the Queen's
;   loop and arena are the Queen's. A lesson may open any widget: that is COURSE_WIDGETS, a second link.
; - Petals: T27 OS has 27 petals in 3 realms of 9 (specs/t27f/petal_menu.t27). Owner: CHAT moves to the
;   THIRD petal (index 2) and the pair chat + commander lives there; each home gets a petal tab. Default:
;   CHAT and LOGS swap places, and the homes take petals 19..25 of the third realm in the order t27a, t27b,
;   t27c, t27f, t27o, t27t, t27u. The Queen's tab is the CHAT petal. ABOUT stays at 26. Moving a home is one
;   edit to HOME_PETAL and to WORLD_NAMES in petal_menu.t27 (the one definition of the names). The seven worlds REELS .. COMMUNITY give up their petals.
; Not established from evidence (so not guessed): what "commander" is, since the repository names no such
; component; whether the tri-fpga-* casts belong to t27c or to the `tri` CLI (filed under t27c because
; `tri fpga` drives `t27c silicon`); which widget a t27a, t27b, t27f or t27o page would be (the gallery has
; none: those four homes show 0 widgets, which is a measurement and not a gap in the table).
; ASCII only (L3), English only (LANG-EN).
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

module T27osHomes;

use t27f::petal_menu::WORLD_NAMES;
use t27f::petal_menu::PETAL_COUNT;
use t27f::petal_menu::PETAL_NONE;
use t27os::session_store::csv_field;
use t27os::session_store::put_bytes;
use t27os::session_store::put_dec;

